<title>USA: Valhi to post gain on fast food unit sale.</title>
<headline>Valhi to post gain on fast food unit sale.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Valhi Inc said on Thursday that it expects to report a pretax gain of $24 million from the sale of its Sybra fast food operations.</p>
<p>The proposed sale will be accomplished in simultaneous dealsthat will include the sale of 63 properties plus 10 leaseholds to U.S. Restaurant Properties for $45 million and the sale of 100 percent of Sybra's stock to I.C.H. Corp for $39.7 million, Valhi said.</p>
<p>Valhi said it will use $23.7 million of the proceeds from the I.C.H. deal to repay Sybra's indebtedness.  </p>
<p>Valhi said the deals are subject to due diligence, arrangements for purchaser financing and certain third party consents.</p>
